<article class="env-definition" id="0E6Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E6Q">Definition <span data-tag="0E6Q">109.19.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a family of curves with Cohen-Macaulay fibres equidimensional of dimension $1$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/0E1F" data-tag="0E1F">109.8.2</a>). Then the $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \omega _{X/S} = H^{-1}(\omega _{X/S}^\bullet )  \]
</div>
  <p> studied in Lemma <a href="/tag/0E6P" data-tag="0E6P">109.19.1</a> is called the <em>relative dualizing sheaf</em> of $f$. </p>
</article>